  "result": "Perfect! All 240 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the overdue invoices report:\n\n**Created src/reports.js with overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf):**\n- Returns array of overdue invoices: [{ number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }]\n- Filters to include only invoices with:\n  - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n  - dueDate strictly before asOf (not on or after)\n- Calculates:\n  - daysOverdue: days between dueDate and asOf using daysBetween()\n  - due: amount owed using balanceDue() (accounts for payments, VAT, discounts, vouchers)\n- Sorts by daysOverdue descending (most overdue first)\n- Does not mutate input invoices\n\n**Added 24 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Empty invoices list\n- No overdue invoices\n- Single and multiple overdue invoices\n- Status filtering (draft excluded, paid excluded, issued/partially_paid included)\n- Date filtering (exact due date excluded, one day overdue included)\n- Correct daysOverdue calculation\n- Correct due calculation (including VAT, discounts, vouchers, payments)\n- Sorting by daysOverdue descending (most overdue first)\n- Multiple customers\n- Invoices spanning years\n- Large daysOverdue values\n- Complex invoice mix with various states\n- Input immutability\n- Edge cases (same daysOverdue, same due date)\n\nAll 240 tests passing.",
